    title: "Arrests made after visit from former US President Biden",
    summary: "Joe Biden was in Dublin to see his son Hunter awarded the Gold Medal for Outstanding Contribution for Public Discourse",
    preview: "At least two arrests have been made following a surprise visit from former US President Joe Biden to Trinity College in Dublin on Tuesday. Biden was accompanied by former first lady Jill Biden as they attended a ceremony where their son Hunter was awarded the Gold Medal for Outstanding Contribution for Public Discourse. During the trio's visit to the College Historical Society groups of pro-Palestinian protesters gathered, some of whom were detained by gardaÃ (Irish police).",
    body: "At least two arrests have been made following a surprise visit from former US President Joe Biden to Trinity College in Dublin on Tuesday.\n\nBiden was accompanied by former first lady Jill Biden as they attended a ceremony where their son Hunter was awarded the Gold Medal for Outstanding Contribution for Public Discourse.\n\nDuring the trio's visit to the College Historical Society groups of pro-Palestinian protesters gathered, some of whom were detained by gardaÃ (Irish police).\n\nAs Biden and his family left the venue, some of the people moved forward and objects were thrown, Irish broadcaster RTÃ has reported.\n\nA number of garda officers and public order unit vans were on site as at least two arrests were made.\n\nIn 2024 Hunter Biden was convicted of gun and tax crimes in in the US but was later pardoned by his father while he was still president.\n\nIt made him the first child of a sitting president to be a convicted of a crime.\n\nAllow X content?\n\nThis article contains content provided by X. We ask for your permission before anything is loaded, as they may be using cookies and other technologies. You may want to read Xs cookie policy, external and privacy policy, external before accepting. To view this content choose accept and continueâ.\n\nPrevious recipients of the award include former Irish president Michael D Higgins, Bob Geldof, Patti Smith, Julian Assange and Desmond Tutu.\n\nThe former US president and his family also met with the Taoiseach (Irish prime minister) Micheál Martin.\n\nMartin said on X that he had been pleased to welcome the family and that they reflected on Biden's \"strong Irish roots\".\n\nRelated topics\n\n- Published2 December 2024\n\n- Published10 November 2020\n\n- Published17 March 2022",
