    title: "UN peacekeepers say came they under fire in southern Lebanon",
    summary: "UN peacekeepers say came they under fire in southern Lebanon The United Nations peacekeeping force in Lebanon (Unifil) said on Tuesday that one of its patrols came under fire in the country's south, without saying who was responsible. The force, whose mandate in Lebanon expires at the end of this year, said the patrol \"was fired upon with about a dozen rounds\" near Wadi Jilu and returned fire, after which the shooting stopped. It reported no casualties and called for an investigation. \"We reiterate the obligation under international law for all actors to ensure the safety and security of UN personnel and property at all times,\" it said. Israel continues attacking southern Lebanon and occupies parts of its territory despite a ceasefire that took effect on 17 April and that was renewed on 26 June.",
    preview: "UN peacekeepers say came they under fire in southern Lebanon The United Nations peacekeeping force in Lebanon (Unifil) said on Tuesday that one of its patrols came under fire in the country's south, without saying who was responsible. The force, whose mandate in Lebanon expires at the end of this year, said the patrol \"was fired upon with about a dozen rounds\" near Wadi Jilu and returned fire, after which the shooting stopped. It reported no casualties and called for an investigation.",
    body: "UN peacekeepers say came they under fire in southern Lebanon The United Nations peacekeeping force in Lebanon (Unifil) said on Tuesday that one of its patrols came under fire in the country's south, without saying who was responsible. The force, whose mandate in Lebanon expires at the end of this year, said the patrol \"was fired upon with about a dozen rounds\" near Wadi Jilu and returned fire, after which the shooting stopped.\n\nIt reported no casualties and called for an investigation. \"We reiterate the obligation under international law for all actors to ensure the safety and security of UN personnel and property at all times,\" it said. Israel continues attacking southern Lebanon and occupies parts of its territory despite a ceasefire that took effect on 17 April and that was renewed on 26 June.",
